  "concept_key": "legends.card.livermore",
  "title": "Legend 01: Jesse Livermore",
  "hook": "Made $1 million in a day. Went bankrupt more than once.",
  "takeaway": "Jesse Livermore taught himself to read markets from prices, won big in the 1907 panic and the 1929 crash, and built his method around the pivotal point: wait for a key price to break, add only while the trade works, then sit tight. He lost fortunes by breaking those rules: following a friend's cotton tips, buying more as cotton fell, and putting money into businesses outside trading. His 1940 rules are the lessons those losses paid for.",
  "learn": [
    "Who Jesse Livermore was: a self-taught trader who made fortunes in the 1907 panic and the 1929 crash, and why traders still call him a legend.",
    "His pivotal point: wait for a key price to break before buying, add only while the trade works, then sit tight.",
    "Why he lost his fortunes: he followed a friend's tips, kept buying a falling market, and lost money in businesses outside trading.",
    "His rules: don't jump in early, never add to a loser, trust your rules over tips, take some profit out."
  ],
  "glossary": {
    "pivotal point": "a price that starts the move"
  },
  "question": null,
  "emotion": "awe at a $1 million day, the wince of watching a master break his own rules, then respect: his losses became the rules we still use",
